msgid "Membership of a representation model in a RepresentationModelNodeGroup (EM16-RMNG): the models that together form one named set published under a single Document — «Survey 2015» under D.01, «Reconstruction» under D.09. THE GROUP SITS BESIDE, IT DOES NOT REPLACE: every member keeps its own epoch edges (has\\_first\\_epoch / survive\\_in\\_epoch) and the Document keeps its DIRECT has\\_representation\\_model edges to each model. This edge is added on top and never put in between, so a consumer that ignores it reads exactly what it read before. Membership is a TAG axis like is\\_in\\_functional\\_unit and is\\_in\\_location — the member carries the edge and the group claims nothing of it — and m:n like them (E.D., 23 Oct 2026; 1:1 until connections 1.6.42): a model may belong to SEVERAL containers — a model of «Survey 2015» can also be in «Reconstruction, 2nd c. AD». The epochs stay on each model: the default epochs an EM Tools container carries are a convenience of the scene, written on its models, never a statement of the group. A group may legally be EMPTY and may legally have no Document: both are states the RM Manager UI already shows, and neither is validated away."
msgstr ""

